    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1519">

                <pb facs="0979" n="863" xml:id="pg863"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/254.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the Secretary of State.</hi><anchor
                        n="138" xml:id="d1519-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 494.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    British Vice Consul in this city has called my attention privately to the
                    circumstance that General Villa has ordered the sequestration of the Hacienda de
                    los Remedios, the property of the widow of the late William S. Benton, the
                    British subject who was murdered by Villa or his agents at Juarez in February
                    last, and has asked my aid in preventing the consummation of the act now
                    projected. I enclose herewith a copy of Villa’s order in the case.</p>
                <p>As I am informed, there is no cloud upon the title to the property in so far as
                    Mrs. Benton is concerned.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marion Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d1519-a1.xml" xpointer="d1519-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1519-f1" n="138" type="source" xml:id="d1519-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the British Ambassador June 16, 1914.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
